    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d741">

                <pb facs="0712" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1120</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Tiflis</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-02-20T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                                1918, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 12, 10 p.m. British military agent, Caucasus, reports to his
                    Government that three Americans were recently in Tiflis who proposed to
                    subsidize Georgia with view to declaration of autonomy.</p>
                <p>Advise Department fully and promptly facts of this report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
